HST Office: Writer aligns a selected picture like a word processor, and the left page margin
selects lines.

- With a picture, embedded object or drawing shape (also a group) selected, Left / Center /
  Right (Home tab, Ctrl+L/E/R, sidebar, context menu, Picture / Shape tab) are enabled and
  show their state. An object anchored as character aligns its paragraph; any other anchor
  centres or aligns the object on the text area of its anchor. One undo step
  (sw/source/uibase/hst/imagealign.cxx).
- In the left margin beside plain body text the pointer is a right-pointing arrow; a click
  selects the line, a double click the paragraph, a drag whole lines, a triple click or
  Ctrl+click the whole document. Tables, footnotes, headers/footers, objects and the comment
  sidebar keep their own handling; the hit test is a few rectangle checks on the visible
  pages (sw/source/uibase/hst/marginlineselect.cxx).

